────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Colledanchise and Ogren, Behavior Trees in Robotics and AI: An Introduction
(CRC Press 2018; arXiv 1709.00084) - https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.00084
    Cited, not copied. This is the textbook chapters 1 to 12 teach from: the
    node definitions, algorithms 1 to 3, the memory node caution, the
    behavior tree versus finite state machine argument and the design
    chapter. The interpreter in src/bt/ is asserted against algorithms 1 to
    3 directly in scripts/check-bt.mjs, so the citation is checked, not just
    stated.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
BehaviorTree.CPP - https://www.behaviortree.dev/ - MIT, Davide Faconti and
contributors.
    No code from the library is used anywhere in this course. Its
    documentation is cited: the Sequence and Fallback comparison tables
    define the memory and keep modes taught in chapters 3, 4 and 7, and the
    blackboard chapter follows its ports model.

